 "Header": {
  "BPX": "1.0.0",
  "Title": "Tesla-like NMC811/graphite 4680 cylindrical cell",
  "Description": "Parameter set for a 4680 cylindrical cell with an NMC811/graphite chemistry. Geometry and the phase inventory are identified in this work from the teardown of Ank et al. (2023, doi:10.1149/1945-7111/ad14d0) and Battery Design's public 4680 data; the electrochemistry is transferred from the LG M50 parameterisation of Chen et al. (2020, doi:10.1149/1945-7111/ab9050); electrolyte transport is Nyman et al. (2008, doi:10.1016/j.electacta.2008.04.023). The positive-electrode diffusivity, its activation energy and the anode window are CALIBRATED (paper 1 v2, Section 5.1, 1 Oct 2026) on the open 1C and 2C charge test of Ank et al. (2023, Fig. 16): can temperature and charge at 4.2 V, Nelder-Mead on a normalised least-squares cost. Result: diffusion time r_s^2/D_s = 8031 s (within x1.2 of the transferred Chen2020 value), E_a,Ds = 11.0 kJ/mol, anode theta0 = 0.700. The calibration also identified a holder contact heat of 0.94 mOhm outside the voltage path (0.5 mOhm per terminal, as Ank et al. estimate); it is a property of their holder and is NOT in this file. The entropic coefficient is the average over the working window of O'Regan et al. (2022, doi:10.1016/j.electacta.2022.140700); the solver uses the function of stoichiometry. The stoichiometry windows are calibrated to the cut-off voltages: OCV(100 %) = 4.2 V and a C/20 discharge to 2.5 V delivering 22.31 Ah (Ank et al.), with the Chen2020 OCPs and the loadings kept. BPX has no field for a provenance tag, for the closure checks, or for the wound-cell thermal network; those are in parameters_nmc.csv and in the released modules. VERSION 1.2 (1 Oct 2026): the calibrated values above (version 1.1 carried r_s^2/D_s = 700 s, E_a,Ds = 25 kJ/mol, theta0 = 0.701). VERSION 1.1 (27 Sep 2026) corrected the version 1.0 files, which carried the solid conductivity sigma instead of the effective eps_s*sigma the solver uses. Licence: CC BY 4.0.",
  "References": "Chen et al. 2020; Ank et al. 2023; Nyman et al. 2008; O'Regan et al. 2022.",
  "Model": "DFN"
 },
